const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"同样的利润，能否同样持续",en:"Can equal earnings persist differently?"},body:{zh:"Sloan把当期利润拆成应计与现金流部分，研究它们对未来利润的含义是否不同，以及价格是否充分区分这种差别。问题不是简单地把应计项目判成坏消息，而是考察会计组成与持续性之间的联系。",en:"Sloan separates earnings into accrual and cash-flow components, asking whether their persistence differs and whether prices reflect that difference. Accruals are not simply classified as bad news; the question concerns the information in earnings composition."}},{title:{zh:"30年的美国公司数据",en:"Thirty years of US company data"},body:{zh:"论文将1993版Compustat与CRSP文件连接，使用1962—1991年财务资料，最终有40,679个公司年度观察。样本筛选要求必要财务项目、股票收益和后续利润可得；银行与保险等缺少所需应计资料的公司不在这一测量范围内。这不是全市场无条件样本。",en:"The study joins the 1993 Compustat and CRSP files, using financial statements for 1962–1991 and 40,679 firm-years. Required accounting items, returns and subsequent earnings determine inclusion. Banks and insurers lack the necessary accrual data in this setup, so the sample is not unconditional market coverage."},reference:{url:"https://www.cuhk.edu.hk/acy2/workshop/June2009Wasley/1996TAR).pdf",label:{zh:"原文第III节：样本形成",en:"Original §III: sample formation"}}},{title:{zh:"应计口径不是随手相减",en:"Accrual measurement is specific"},body:{zh:"由于现金流量表规则只覆盖样本末期，作者用资产负债表与利润表项目构造经营应计：流动资产变动扣现金，减去调整短期债务和应付税后的流动负债变动，再扣折旧摊销。利润采用折旧后的经营利润，现金部分由利润减应计得到，不能直接替换成任意净利润与现金流字段。",en:"Because cash-flow-statement reporting covers only the sample's final years, operating accruals are reconstructed from balance-sheet changes and depreciation. Earnings use operating income after depreciation; the cash component is the residual after accruals. Arbitrary net-income and cash-flow fields are not interchangeable with these definitions."},reference:{url:"https://www.cuhk.edu.hk/acy2/workshop/June2009Wasley/1996TAR).pdf",label:{zh:"原文第III节：变量定义",en:"Original §III: variable measurement"}}},{title:{zh:"分别检验持续性与定价",en:"Test persistence and pricing separately"},body:{zh:"论文先研究两个组成部分对未来利润的持续性，再检验价格中隐含的预期是否充分区分它们。进一步观察后续异常收益及其是否集中在未来业绩公告附近。这样能把会计关系、价格解释与信息揭示时间联系起来，但每一层都有各自的模型假设。",en:"The tests separate earnings persistence from expectations embedded in prices, then examine subsequent abnormal returns and their concentration around later earnings announcements. Accounting relations, pricing interpretation and information timing are connected, but each layer retains its own assumptions."}},{title:{zh:"发现应怎样理解",en:"How to interpret the finding"},body:{zh:"作者报告应计部分的持续性低于现金部分，价格表现与投资者未充分区分这两者相一致。原文中的历史异常收益是支持这一解释的证据，不是今天可获得同样收益的保证；异常收益也依赖基准模型，不能直接叫作无风险利润。",en:"The paper reports lower persistence for the accrual component and price behavior consistent with incomplete differentiation. Historical abnormal returns support that interpretation; they do not promise a current payoff. Abnormal performance also depends on the benchmark and is not risk-free profit."}},{title:{zh:"读完后先准备版本面板",en:"Prepare a versioned panel first"},body:{zh:"编辑建议：从原文第III节逐项映射会计定义，保留单位、合并范围与报告版本。财年末不等于信息可得日，最新重述值也不能倒填历史。若历史版本或发布日期不足，先把缺口列清，再用时点一致教程验证选择规则，不要先做组合再补解释。",en:"Editorial application: map each Section III definition, preserving units, consolidation scope and filing versions. Fiscal year-end is not availability; latest restatements cannot be backfilled as historical knowledge. Expose missing vintage or release evidence before moving beyond the point-in-time preparation exercise."}}],readerLimits:{zh:"会计准则、行业范围、存活筛选与披露时间都会影响迁移；应计高低本身不是公司质量定论。",en:"Accounting rules, industry coverage, survival filters and disclosure timing affect transferability. Accrual magnitude alone is not a verdict on company quality."}};export{e as default};
